# Finding: the trap is WIDER than the design record states. _strip_comment fires on ' #',
# and every to-tickets heading ('  ## What to build') contains ' #' — so the slice's own
# section headings, not just an incidental ' #47', vanish from the parsed value. The raw
# workflow.yaml text is the only truth for an embedded block, and the ' #' WARN therefore
# fires on EVERY sliced brief rather than on the rare one. Both consequences are load-
# bearing, and both are now carried by the ported §A4 in validate_workflow.py: it compares
# raw text only, and emits the ' #' WARN once per embedded block as a standing note.
